150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 396 0 R
/E (Aggressive hardware prefetching can pollute the Last-Level Cache by filling it with speculatively fetched blocks that are never accessed. In shared multicore LLCs, this pollution is amplified as multiple cores prefetch simultaneously, causing eviction of useful demand data and increasing miss rates.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
